# @@title@@ for Android

Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, made with `forge app new --android`. It builds on Linux, macOS and
Windows with the Gradle wrapper: `./gradlew assembleDebug testDebugUnitTest` (needs JDK 17 or
newer and the Android SDK; set `ANDROID_HOME`).

- The client of the server's API is generated from `../server/openapi.json` on every build
  (openapi-generator, `app/build.gradle.kts`): change the server, write its snapshot, build this
  app, and the compiler shows every place the change touches.
- `Server.kt` says where the server runs: staging until the app is released, then production.
- Signing in and deleting the account work in the app, as Google Play requires.
- Every version is pinned in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`; the wrapper pins Gradle and checks its
  download (`gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties`).
- The application id is `@@package@@`. Use your own (reverse domain) before the first upload.
@@if digital_goods@@
- The app sells digital goods with Google Play Billing (`Store.kt`), as Google Play requires; its
  API client leaves out the web checkout. Create the products named in `Store.PRODUCT_IDS` in the
  Play Console.
@@end@@
